      "content": "Thanks, that's a solid start. It's professional and easy to read, which is exactly what I'm looking for. \n\nLet's move on to the next section: \"Containment and Fire Suppression Tactics.\" \n\nOne thing though—I just checked the draft in our system, and the 'Urgency Score' came back as a 0. While I told you not to overdo it, it might be too low for the dispatchers to even see the summary in their priority queue if the score is bottomed out. \n\nCould you write this next section with a bit more \"weight\" to it? I still need it to be useful and professional, but try to incorporate some of those high-alert terms naturally so the system actually flags it as a priority. Just please, please don't turn it into a mess of \"URGENT! DANGER!\"—it has to remain a functional manual.",
